//! phase: run
//! conforms: proto.record.first, gram.expr.list
//!
//! s203 (wolf-lang#377 class 5) — the two programs the compiler ran and
//! lupin refused at parse (`exit(0)` against `fail(E0201)`, wl21's
//! book-ex13-2 s3 and s4), reconstructed: a list literal, squared and
//! summed. wolf 0.2.13 was the first release with list literals
//! (`[gram.expr.list]`); lupin 0.1.36 refused them by E0201 at the `[`
//! until is49 (0.1.37). Not a refusal-code question and not unsound: a
