## corpus/rows/unit_discard_fallible_body_stmt.lu
//! check: run(exit=0, stdout="after if\n7\n")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: type.unit.context, type.unit.discard, diag.sev.warn
//! warns: W0601
//!
//! s207 (wolf-lang#541) — an else-less `if` as a STATEMENT in a
//! fallible function is still a unit context: its raising then-block is
//! discarded, warned, and the function goes on to its own tail. Native,
//! release and lupin print `after if` and `7`; the checked machine let
//! the row leave `g` and the caller's `else` printed `0` until s207.
