## corpus/typecheck/cast_narrow_wrapping_truncates.lu
//! check: run(exit=0, stdout="44 255 4294967295 -56 127 255 0")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: type.numlit.cast.narrow, type.numlit.cast.wrap
//!
//! Truncation is spelled through the wrapping family
//! (`[type.numlit.cast.narrow]`): the cast INTO `wrapping[T]` masks to
//! the width and never traps (#131), and the cast back OUT keeps the
//! held value, which by then fits. Signed wrapping widths read their
//! bits as signed: `200 as wrapping[i8] as i8` is `-56`. Until kw03 the
//! checked machine range-checked the mask instead of the value, so the
